SHEET 1 880 680
TEXT -16 -40 Left 2 ;TS808 tone + level stage - SushiDSP spec D6c. Probe node: out.
TEXT -16 -8 Left 2 ;Traced from the ElectroSmash TS808 tone/volume schematic and R.G. Keen,\n"The Technology of the Tube Screamer" (geofex.com), section "Tone and volume\ncontrol stages". Both are cited in README.md.
TEXT -16 56 Left 2 !.param AMP=100m TONE=0.5 LEVEL=1\nV1 src 0 SINE(0 {AMP} 1k) AC 1\n* 1k into 220n: the passive low-pass ahead of the tone stage, 723 Hz\nR7 src a 1k\nC5 a 0 220n\n* the 4V5 bias return, an AC ground\nR9 a 0 10k\n* 20k tone pot from the + input to the - input; its wiper drives 220n into 220\nRta a tw {max(20k*TONE,1m)}\nRtb tw inv {max(20k*(1-TONE),1m)}\nC6 tw tm 220n\nR8 tm 0 220\n* non-inverting stage: 1k from the output back to the - input\nR11 inv tsout 1k\nEop tsout 0 a inv 1e6\n* 1u output cap, 1k series resistor, 100k level pot; the wiper is the probe\nC7 tsout lt 1u\nR12 lt ltop 1k\nRla ltop out {max(100k*(1-LEVEL),1m)}\nRlb out 0 {max(100k*LEVEL,1m)}\n.step param TONE list 0.1 0.5 0.9\n.options plotwinsize=0
TEXT -16 560 Left 2 ;ac dec 40 10 20k
TEXT -16 592 Left 2 ;tran 0 40m 20m 1u
TEXT -16 632 Left 2 ;The two lines above are the analyses tools/spice/export.py enables\nby rewriting their leading ';' into '!.' - exactly one at a time.
